#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:4
msgid "Route this mockup request to the `ui-designer` agent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:6
msgid "Renderer Selection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:8
msgid "**Do not derive the renderer yourself.** The CLI does it. Run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:10
msgid "hero spec mock detect [--renderer=<flag-if-user-passed-one>]\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:14
msgid "Read the single line of JSON it prints. Fields:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:15
msgid ""
"`renderer` — `\"html\"` or `\"swiftui\"`. **Use this value verbatim** — "
"pass it to `ui-designer` as the chosen renderer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:16
msgid "`reason` — one-sentence rationale for the announce step below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:17
msgid ""
"`signals` — what fired (e.g. `\"Package.swift\"`, `\"MyApp.xcodeproj\"`, "
"`\"12 .swift files at root\"`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:18
msgid "`toolchain_ok` / `toolchain_path` — whether `swiftc` was found."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:19
msgid "`config_override` — set when `hero.json` `mockups.renderer` won."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:20
msgid "`explicit_flag` — echoed back when the user passed `--renderer=...`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:21
msgid ""
"`conflict` — non-null when the choice is suspicious (e.g. "
"`--renderer=html` on a Swift project, or `--renderer=swiftui` with no "
"`swiftc`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:23
msgid ""
"If `conflict` is non-null, **halt** — do not proceed to generation. "
"Surface the conflict message to the user and ask them to confirm:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:25
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Renderer choice conflict.\n"
"{conflict message from detect output}\n"
"Confirm one:\n"
"  [keep flag]    use {explicit_flag} as requested\n"
"  [use detected] override my flag and use the auto-detected renderer\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:33
msgid "Only proceed once the user picks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:35
msgid "Announce step (mandatory, before any generation)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:37
msgid ""
"Before delegating to `ui-designer`, emit this one-line announcement as "
"user-visible output:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:39
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Renderer: {renderer} — reason: {reason} — swiftc: {toolchain_path or "
"\"unavailable\"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:43
msgid ""
"This is the gate that catches wrong picks in-turn — the user sees the "
"choice before any files are written. Skipping it is the bug this command "
"was designed to fix."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:45
msgid ""
"For fallback cases (Swift signals present but no `swiftc`), the announce "
"becomes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:47
msgid "Renderer: HTML (SwiftUI unavailable — swiftc not found)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:51
msgid "Tell the ui-designer which renderer to use and which skill to load:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:52
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**HTML:** Load `html-mockup-generation` skill. Output: "
"`.hero/mocks/{slug}/index.html`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:53
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**SwiftUI:** Load `swiftui-mockup-renderer` skill. Output: "
"`.hero/mocks/{slug}/MockView.swift` + `screenshot.png` + `screenshot-"
"dark.png` + `index.html` (viewer)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:55
msgid "Workflow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:57
msgid "The ui-designer will:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:58
msgid "Read the spec (if a slug is provided) or parse the free-text description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:59
msgid "Identify the key screens, components, and interactions needed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:60
msgid "Generate the mockup using the selected renderer:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:61
msgid "**HTML:** Self-contained `index.html` with embedded CSS and JS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:62
msgid ""
"**SwiftUI:** `MockView.swift` source → compile → capture PNG screenshots "
"(light + dark)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:63
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Save to `.hero/mocks/{slug}/` (or `.hero/mocks/_adhoc/{summary-slug}/` "
"for free-text)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:64
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"If a spec slug was provided, append (or update on `--iterate`) a `## "
"Mockups` entry in the originating spec at "
"`.hero/planning/features/{slug}/spec.md` or "
"`.hero/planning/bugs/{slug}/spec.md` (or `.hero/specs/{slug}/spec.md` if "
"already archived). Entry format:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:65
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"HTML: `- [{Name}](.hero/mocks/{slug}/index.html) — YYYY-MM-DD — one-line "
"description`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:66
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"SwiftUI: `- [{Name}](.hero/mocks/{slug}/screenshot.png) — YYYY-MM-DD — "
"SwiftUI native render`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:68
msgid ""
"If the user provides `--iterate` feedback, read the existing mockup first"
" and modify it based on the feedback rather than regenerating from "
"scratch. On iterate, update the matching `## Mockups` entry's date in "
"place rather than appending a duplicate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:70
msgid "**Output requirements (HTML renderer):**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:71
msgid "Single self-contained `index.html` — no external dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:72
msgid "Professional, clean design with modern CSS (flexbox/grid)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:73
msgid "Basic interactivity where appropriate (tabs, modals, dropdowns)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:74
msgid "Responsive layout (works on mobile and desktop)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:75
msgid "HTML comment header with spec slug, date, and description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:77
msgid "**Output requirements (SwiftUI renderer):**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:78
msgid "Single self-contained `MockView.swift` — no SPM dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:79
msgid "Real SwiftUI components, SF Symbols, system colors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:80
msgid "Both light and dark mode screenshots captured"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:81
msgid "Viewer `index.html` wrapping the PNGs with light/dark toggle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:83
msgid "**Surface outputs — orchestrator responsibility (READ THIS):**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:85
msgid ""
"The `ui-designer` runs as a subagent. **The subagent's return value is "
"NOT visible to the user.** When the Agent tool completes, you (the "
"orchestrator running this command) MUST emit a clickable file inventory "
"in your *own* user-facing text response — do not assume the subagent's "
"links reach the user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:87
msgid ""
"To make this reliable, instruct the `ui-designer` (in the prompt you send"
" it) to terminate its return text with a machine-parseable block:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:89
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"<MOCKUP_FILES>\n"
".hero/mocks/{slug}/index.html|Mockup name|primary\n"
".hero/mocks/{slug}/screenshot.png|Screenshot — light|image\n"
".hero/mocks/{slug}/screenshot-dark.png|Screenshot — dark|image\n"
".hero/mocks/{slug}/MockView.swift|SwiftUI source|source\n"
".hero/planning/features/{slug}/spec.md|Spec (Mockups section "
"updated)|spec\n"
"</MOCKUP_FILES>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:99
msgid ""
"Parse that block from the tool result and re-emit it in your final "
"response as a markdown list of clickable links:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:101
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Mockups generated:**\n"
"- [Mockup name](.hero/mocks/{slug}/index.html) — primary\n"
"- [Screenshot — light](.hero/mocks/{slug}/screenshot.png)\n"
"- [Screenshot — dark](.hero/mocks/{slug}/screenshot-dark.png)\n"
"- [SwiftUI source](.hero/mocks/{slug}/MockView.swift)\n"
"- [Spec updated](.hero/planning/features/{slug}/spec.md) — `## Mockups` "
"entry appended\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:110
msgid ""
"If the subagent did not return a `<MOCKUP_FILES>` block, fall back to "
"scanning its response text for `.hero/mocks/...` paths and listing those."
" Either way, the inventory must appear in YOUR response, not just the "
"subagent's."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/mock.md:112
msgid ""
"**Spec write-back check:** If a spec slug was provided, verify the "
"subagent updated the spec's `## Mockups` section. If the inventory does "
"not include the spec path, read the spec file yourself and append the "
"entry before finishing."
msgstr ""

